\s1 A Call to Repentance
\r (\ref Jeremiah 3:11–25|JER 3:11-25\ref*; \ref Hosea 14:1–3|HOS 14:1-3\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb of the second|שְׁתַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Darius|לְדָרְיָ֑וֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָה֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Berechiah|בֶּ֣רֶכְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Iddo|עִדּ֥וֹ\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*:
\p \v 2 “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb was very|קָֽצֶף׃\rb* \rb angry|קָצַ֧ף\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 3 \rb So tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb the people|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Return|שׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and I will return|וְאָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*.’
\p \v 4 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be|תִּהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb like your fathers|כַאֲבֹֽתֵיכֶ֡ם\rb*, \rb to whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the former|הָרִֽאשֹׁנִ֜ים\rb* \rb prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֨ים\rb* \rb proclaimed|קָרְאֽוּ־\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶם֩\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אָמַר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*: ‘\rb Turn|שׁ֤וּבוּ\rb* \rb now|נָא֙\rb* \rb from your evil|הָרָעִ֔ים\rb* \rb ways|מִדַּרְכֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and|הָֽרָעִ֑ים\rb* \rb deeds|וּמַעֲלִילֵיכֶם\rb*.’
\p \rb But they did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמְע֛וּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb or pay attention|הִקְשִׁ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Where|אַיֵּה־\rb*\rb |הֵ֑ם\rb* \rb are your fathers now|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*? \rb And the prophets|וְהַ֨נְּבִאִ֔ים\rb*, \rb do they live|יִֽחְיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb forever|הַלְעוֹלָ֖ם\rb*? \v 6 \rb But|אַ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb did not|הֲל֥וֹא\rb* \rb My words|דְּבָרַ֣י\rb* \rb and My statutes|וְחֻקַּ֗י\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוִּ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My servants|עֲבָדַ֣י\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb*, \rb overtake|הִשִּׂ֖יגוּ\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*? \rb They repented|וַיָּשׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*, ‘\rb Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb purposed|זָמַ֜ם\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb to us|לָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb according to our ways|כִּדְרָכֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and deeds|וּכְמַ֣עֲלָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb He has done|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb to us|אִתָּֽנוּ׃ס\rb*.’”
\s1 The Vision of the Horses
\p \v 7 \rb On the twenty-fourth|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֜ה\rb* \rb day|בְּיוֹם֩\rb* \rb of the eleventh|לְעַשְׁתֵּֽי־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb month|חֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*,\rb |הוּא־\rb* \rb the month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Shebat|שְׁבָ֔ט\rb*,\f + \fr 1:7 \fqa Shebat \ft is the eleventh month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of January and February.\f* \rb in the second|שְׁתַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Darius|לְדָרְיָ֑וֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָה֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Berechiah|בֶּ֣רֶכְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Iddo|עִדּ֥וֹא\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb I looked out|רָאִ֣יתִי׀\rb* \rb into the night|הַלַּ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb riding|רֹכֵב֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a red|אָדֹ֔ם\rb* \rb horse|ס֣וּס\rb*. \rb He|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb was standing|עֹמֵ֔ד\rb* \rb among|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the myrtle trees|הַהֲדַסִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the hollow|בַּמְּצֻלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and behind him|וְאַחֲרָיו֙\rb* \rb were red|אֲדֻמִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb sorrel|שְׂרֻקִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb and white|וּלְבָנִֽים׃\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִ֣ים\rb*.
\p \v 9 “\rb What|מָה־\rb* \rb are these|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb*?” \rb I asked|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*.
\p \rb And the angel|הַמַּלְאָךְ֙\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֔י\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will show|אַרְאֶ֖ךָּ\rb* \rb you what|מָה־\rb* \rb they are|הֵ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |אֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Then the man|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb standing|הָעֹמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb among|בֵּין־\rb* \rb the myrtle trees|הַהַדַסִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb explained|וַיַּ֗עַן\rb*, “\rb They|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the ones|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has sent|שָׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb to patrol|לְהִתְהַלֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb the earth|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb And the riders answered|וַֽיַּעֲנ֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb who was standing|הָֽעֹמֵד֙\rb* \rb among|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the myrtle trees|הַהֲדַסִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*, “\rb We have patrolled|הִתְהַלַּ֣כְנוּ\rb* \rb the earth|בָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and behold|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb is at rest|יֹשֶׁ֥בֶת\rb* \rb and tranquil|וְשֹׁקָֽטֶת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb Then the angel|מַלְאַךְ־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמַר֒\rb*\rb |וַיַּ֣עַן\rb*, “\rb How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַ֗י\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb will You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb withhold mercy|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |תְרַחֵ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You have been angry|זָעַ֔מְתָּה\rb* \rb these|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 13 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb spoke|וַיַּ֣עַן\rb* \rb kind|טוֹבִ֑ים\rb*\rb |דְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and comforting|נִחֻמִֽים׃\rb* \rb words|דְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Then the angel|הַמַּלְאָךְ֙\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֔י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb Proclaim|קְרָ֣א\rb* \rb this word|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*: \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: ‘\rb I am very|גְדוֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb jealous|קִנֵּ֧אתִי\rb*\rb |קִנְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb for Jerusalem|לִירוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb and Zion|וּלְצִיּ֖וֹן\rb*, \v 15 \rb but I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am fiercely angry|וְקֶ֤צֶף\rb*\rb |גָּדוֹל֙\rb*\rb |קֹצֵ֔ף\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb that are at ease|הַשַּֽׁאֲנַנִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb For|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb was a little|מְּעָ֔ט\rb* \rb angry|קָצַ֣פְתִּי\rb*, \rb but they|וְהֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb have added to|עָזְר֥וּ\rb* \rb the calamity|לְרָעָֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 1:15 \ft Or \fqa they have overdone the punishment\f*’
\p \v 16 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb I will return|שַׁ֤בְתִּי\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|לִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb with mercy|בְּֽרַחֲמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and there|בָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb My house|בֵּיתִי֙\rb* \rb will be rebuilt|יִבָּ֣נֶה\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and a measuring line|וְקָוָה\rb* \rb will be stretched out|יִנָּטֶ֖ה\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 17 \rb Proclaim|קְרָ֣א\rb* \rb further that|ע֣וֹד׀\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אָמַר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*: ‘\rb My cities|עָרַ֖י\rb* \rb will again|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb overflow|תְּפוּצֶ֥ינָה\rb* \rb with prosperity|מִטּ֑וֹב\rb*; \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb will again|עוֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb comfort|וְנִחַ֨ם\rb* \rb Zion|צִיּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb choose|וּבָחַ֥ר\rb* \rb Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃ס\rb*.’”
\s1 The Vision of the Horns and the Craftsmen
\p \v 18 \rb Then I looked up|וָאֶשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עֵינַ֖י\rb* \rb and saw|וָאֵ֑רֶא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb horns|קְרָנֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb So I asked|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֖י\rb*, “\rb What|מָה־\rb* \rb are these|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb*?”
\p \rb And he told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb These|אֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb are the horns|הַקְּרָנוֹת֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb have scattered|זֵר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Jerusalem|וִירוּשָׁלָֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb showed me|וַיַּרְאֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb craftsmen|חָרָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 “\rb What|מָ֛ה\rb* \rb are these|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb coming|בָאִ֖ים\rb* \rb to do|לַֽעֲשׂ֑וֹת\rb*?” \rb I asked|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb*.
\p \rb And He replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* “\rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the horns|הַקְּרָנ֞וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb scattered|זֵ֣רוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb so that|כְּפִי־\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb one|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb could raise|נָשָׂ֣א\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb*; \rb but the craftsmen|אֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb have come|וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to terrify|לְהַחֲרִ֣יד\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and throw down|לְיַדּ֞וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these horns|קַרְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb* \rb that have lifted up|הַנֹּשְׂאִ֥ים\rb* \rb their horns|קֶ֛רֶן\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb to scatter it|לְזָרוֹתָֽהּ׃ס\rb*.”
\c 2
\s1 The Vision of the Measuring Line
\r (\ref Ezekiel 40:1–4|EZK 40:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then I lifted|וָאֶשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb up my eyes|עֵינַ֛י\rb* \rb and saw|וָאֵ֖רֶא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb with a measuring|מִדָּֽה׃\rb* \rb line|חֶ֥בֶל\rb* \rb in his hand|וּבְיָד֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 2 “\rb Where|אָ֖נָה\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb going|הֹלֵ֑ךְ\rb*?” \rb I asked|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb*.
\p “\rb To measure|לָמֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb and to determine|לִרְא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |כַּמָּֽה־\rb* \rb its width|רָחְבָּ֖הּ\rb*\rb |וְכַמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and length|אָרְכָּֽהּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb Then|וְהִנֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֖י\rb* \rb went forth|יֹצֵ֑א\rb*, \rb and another|אַחֵ֔ר\rb* \rb angel|וּמַלְאָ֣ךְ\rb* \rb came forward|יֹצֵ֖א\rb* \rb to meet him|לִקְרָאתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔ו\rb*, “\rb Run|רֻ֗ץ\rb* \rb and tell|דַּבֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb that|הַלָּ֖ז\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb young man|הַנַּ֥עַר\rb*: ‘\rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb will be a city|תֵּשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb without walls|פְּרָזוֹת֙\rb* \rb because of the multitude|מֵרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb of men|אָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb and livestock|וּבְהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb within it|בְּתוֹכָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb For I|וַאֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb will be|אֶֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb a wall|ח֥וֹמַת\rb* \rb of fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb around it|סָבִ֑יב\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and I will be|אֶֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the glory|וּלְכָב֖וֹד\rb* \rb within it|בְתוֹכָֽהּ׃פ\rb*.’”
\s1 The Redemption of Zion
\r (\ref Hosea 3:1–5|HOS 3:1-5\ref*)
\p \v 6 “\rb Get up|ה֣וֹי\rb*! \rb Get up|ה֗וֹי\rb*! \rb Flee|וְנֻ֛סוּ\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the north|צָפ֖וֹן\rb*,” \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb I have scattered|פֵּרַ֥שְׂתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb you like the four|כְּאַרְבַּ֞ע\rb* \rb winds|רוּח֧וֹת\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֛יִם\rb*,” \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 7 “\rb Get up|ה֥וֹי\rb*, \rb O Zion|צִיּ֖וֹן\rb*! \rb Escape|הִמָּלְטִ֑י\rb*, \rb you who dwell|יוֹשֶׁ֖בֶת\rb* \rb with the Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶֽל׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 8 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֒\rb*\rb |אַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: “\rb After His Glory|כָּב֔וֹד\rb* \rb has sent Me|שְׁלָחַ֕נִי\rb*\f + \fr 2:8 \ft Or \fqa After the Glorious One has sent Me \ft or \fqa After He has honored Me and sent Me\f* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb that have plundered you|הַשֹּׁלְלִ֣ים\rb* —\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb whoever touches|הַנֹּגֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb you|בָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb touches|נֹגֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb the apple|בְּבָבַ֥ת\rb*\f + \fr 2:8 \ft Or \fqa the pupil\f* \rb of His eye|עֵינֽוֹ׃\rb* — \v 9 \rb |כִּ֠י\rb* \rb I will surely|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb wave|מֵנִ֤יף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that they will become|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb plunder|שָׁלָ֖ל\rb* \rb for their own servants|לְעַבְדֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb has sent Me|שְׁלָחָֽנִי׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 10 “\rb Shout for joy|רָנִּ֥י\rb* \rb and be glad|וְשִׂמְחִ֖י\rb*, \rb O Daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֑וֹן\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb*\rb |הִנְנִי־\rb* \rb I am coming|בָ֛א\rb* \rb to dwell|וְשָׁכַנְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb among you|בְתוֹכֵ֖ךְ\rb*,” \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 “\rb On that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֤ים\rb* \rb nations|גוֹיִ֨ם\rb* \rb will join|וְנִלְווּ֩\rb* \rb themselves to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb and they will become|וְהָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb My|לִ֖י\rb* \rb people|לְעָ֑ם\rb*. \rb I will dwell|וְשָׁכַנְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb among you|בְתוֹכֵ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb and you will know|וְיָדַ֕עַתְּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb has sent Me|שְׁלָחַ֥נִי\rb* \rb to you|אֵלָֽיִךְ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will take possession|וְנָחַ֨ל\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb as His portion|חֶלְק֔וֹ\rb* \rb in|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the Holy|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb Land|אַדְמַ֣ת\rb*, \rb and He will once again|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb choose|וּבָחַ֥ר\rb* \rb Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Be silent|הַ֥ס\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb people|בָּשָׂ֖ר\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb He has roused Himself|נֵע֖וֹר\rb* \rb from His holy|קָדְשֽׁוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb dwelling|מִמְּע֥וֹן\rb*.”
\c 3
\s1 The Vision of Joshua the High Priest
\p \v 1 \rb Then the angel showed me|וַיַּרְאֵ֗נִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb the high|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֕ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Or \fqa Angel\ft ; also in verses 3, 4, 5, and 6; corresponding pronouns may also be capitalized.\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb with Satan|וְהַשָּׂטָ֛ן\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft That is, \fqa the Accuser \ft or \fqa the Adversary\ft ; also in verse 2\f* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb his right hand|יְמִינ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to accuse him|לְשִׂטְנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֗ן\rb*: “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb rebukes|יִגְעַ֨ר\rb* \rb you|בְּךָ֙\rb*, \rb Satan|הַשָּׂטָ֔ן\rb*! \rb Indeed, the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb who has chosen|הַבֹּחֵ֖ר\rb* \rb Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb rebukes|וְיִגְעַ֤ר\rb* \rb you|בְּךָ֔\rb*! \rb Is not|הֲל֧וֹא\rb* \rb this man|זֶ֦ה\rb* \rb a firebrand|א֖וּד\rb*\f + \fr 3:2 \ft That is, \fqa a burning stick\f* \rb snatched|מֻצָּ֥ל\rb* \rb from the fire|מֵאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 3 \rb Now Joshua|וִיהוֹשֻׁ֕עַ\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb dressed|לָבֻ֖שׁ\rb* \rb in filthy|צוֹאִ֑ים\rb* \rb garments|בְּגָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb as he stood|וְעֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb So the angel|וַיַּ֣עַן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb those standing|הָעֹמְדִ֤ים\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָיו֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Take off|הָסִ֛ירוּ\rb* \rb his filthy|הַצֹּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb clothes|הַבְּגָדִ֥ים\rb*!”
\p \rb Then he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to Joshua|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb See|רְאֵ֨ה\rb*, \rb I have removed|הֶעֱבַ֤רְתִּי\rb* \rb your iniquity|עֲוֺנֶ֔ךָ\rb*\rb |מֵעָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb and I will clothe|וְהַלְבֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb you|אֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb with splendid robes|מַחֲלָצֽוֹת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Then I said|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb Let them put|יָשִׂ֛ימוּ\rb* \rb a clean|טָה֖וֹר\rb* \rb turban|צָנִ֥יף\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*.” \rb So a clean|הַטָּה֜וֹר\rb* \rb turban|הַצָּנִ֨יף\rb* \rb was placed|וַיָּשִׂימוּ֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb and they clothed him|וַיַּלְבִּשֻׁ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |בְּגָדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb as the angel|וּמַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb stood by|עֹמֵֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb gave this charge|וַיָּ֙עַד֙\rb* \rb to Joshua|בִּיהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 7 “\rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*: ‘\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you walk|תֵּלֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |וְאִ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in My ways|בִּדְרָכַ֤י\rb* \rb and keep|תִשְׁמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb My instructions|מִשְׁמַרְתִּ֣י\rb*, \rb then you|אַתָּה֙\rb*\rb |וְגַם־\rb* \rb will govern|תָּדִ֣ין\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My house|בֵּיתִ֔י\rb* \rb and will also|וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb have charge|תִּשְׁמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb of|אֶת־\rb* \rb My courts|חֲצֵרָ֑י\rb*; \rb and I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb a place|מַהְלְכִ֔ים\rb* \rb among|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb who are standing here|הָעֹמְדִ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Hear|שְֽׁמַֽע־\rb* \rb now|נָ֞א\rb*, \rb O high|הַגָּד֗וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ׀\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and your companions|וְרֵעֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb seated|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb who are indeed|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb a sign|מוֹפֵ֖ת\rb*.\rb |הֵ֑מָּה\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb behold|הִנְנִ֥י\rb*, \rb I am going to bring|מֵבִ֛יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֖י\rb*, \rb the Branch|צֶֽמַח׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb |כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb See|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb the stone|הָאֶ֗בֶן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I have set|נָתַ֙תִּי֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb*; \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb that one|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb stone|אֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb are seven|שִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb eyes|עֵינָ֑יִם\rb*.\f + \fr 3:9 \ft Or \fqa facets\f* \rb Behold|הִנְנִ֧י\rb*, \rb I will engrave on it|מְפַתֵּ֣חַ\rb* \rb an inscription|פִּתֻּחָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and I will remove|וּמַשְׁתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb of this|הַהִ֖יא\rb* \rb land|הָאָֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb in a single|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb*. \v 10 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb you will each invite|תִּקְרְא֖וּ\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb your neighbor|לְרֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb sit under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb your own vine|גֶּ֖פֶן\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb fig tree|תְּאֵנָֽה׃\rb*.’”
\c 4
\s1 The Vision of the Lampstand and Olive Trees
\p \v 1 \rb Then the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֑י\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֕שָׁב\rb* \rb and woke me|וַיְעִירֵ֕נִי\rb*, \rb as a man|כְּאִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is awakened|יֵע֥וֹר\rb* \rb from his sleep|מִשְּׁנָתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 “\rb What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb do you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶ֑ה\rb*?” \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb*.
\p “\rb I see|רָאִ֣יתִי׀\rb* \rb a solid gold|זָהָ֨ב\rb*\rb |כֻּלָּ֜הּ\rb* \rb lampstand|מְנוֹרַת֩\rb*,” \rb I replied|וַיֹּאמֶר\rb*, “\rb with|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb a bowl|וְגֻלָּ֣הּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the top|רֹאשָׁ֗הּ\rb* \rb and seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֤ה\rb* \rb lamps|נֵרֹתֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |שִׁבְעָ֤ה\rb*, \rb with seven|וְשִׁבְעָה֙\rb* \rb spouts|מֽוּצָק֔וֹת\rb* \rb to the lamps|לַנֵּר֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |רֹאשָֽׁהּ׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb There are also two|וּשְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb olive trees|זֵיתִ֖ים\rb* \rb beside it|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb on the right side|מִימִ֣ין\rb* \rb of the bowl|הַגֻּלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and the other|וְאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its left|שְׂמֹאלָֽהּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 “\rb What|מָה־\rb* \rb are these|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb*?” \rb I asked|וָאַ֙עַן֙\rb*\rb |וָֽאֹמַ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֖י\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*.
\p \v 5 “\rb Do you not|הֲל֥וֹא\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֖עְתָּ\rb* \rb what|מָה־\rb* \rb they are|הֵ֣מָּה\rb*?” \rb replied|וַ֠יַּעַן\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֞ךְ\rb*\rb |הַדֹּבֵ֥ר\rb*.
\p “\rb No|לֹ֥א\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb*,” \rb I answered|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb*\rb |וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb So he said to me|וַיַּ֜עַן\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֚ה\rb* \rb is the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֵלַי֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֖ל\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb Not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb by might|בְחַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb by power|בְכֹ֔חַ\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb by My Spirit|בְּרוּחִ֔י\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb What|מִֽי־\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֧ה\rb*, \rb O great|הַגָּד֛וֹל\rb* \rb mountain|הַֽר־\rb*? \rb Before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb you will become a plain|לְמִישֹׁ֑ר\rb*. \rb Then he will bring forth|וְהוֹצִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the capstone|הָאֶ֣בֶן\rb*\rb |הָרֹאשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb accompanied by shouts of|תְּשֻׁא֕וֹת\rb* ‘\rb Grace|חֵ֥ן\rb*, \rb grace|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb to it|לָֽהּ׃פ\rb*!’”
\p \v 8 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 9 “\rb The hands|יְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֗ל\rb* \rb have laid the foundation|יִסְּד֛וּ\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb house|הַבַּ֥יִת\rb*, \rb and his hands|וְיָדָ֣יו\rb* \rb will complete it|תְּבַצַּ֑עְנָה\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וְיָ֣דַעְתָּ֔\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֥נִי\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb has despised|בַז֮\rb* \rb the day|לְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of small things|קְטַנּוֹת֒\rb*? \rb But these|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָה־\rb* \rb eyes|עֵינֵ֣י\rb*\f + \fr 4:10 \ft Or \fqa facets\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb which|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb scan|מְשׁוֹטְטִ֖ים\rb* \rb the whole|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*, \rb will rejoice|וְשָׂמְח֗וּ\rb* \rb when they see|וְרָא֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the plumb line|הָאֶ֧בֶן\rb*\f + \fr 4:10 \ft Or \fqa the chosen capstone\f*\rb |הַבְּדִ֛יל\rb* \rb in the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of Zerubbabel|זְרֻבָּבֶ֖ל\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb Then I asked|וָאַ֖עַן\rb* \rb the angel|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb are the|הָאֵ֔לֶה\rb* \rb two|שְּׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb olive trees|הַזֵּיתִים֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the right|יְמִ֥ין\rb* \rb and left|שְׂמֹאולָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb of the lampstand|הַמְּנוֹרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb*?” \v 12 \rb And I questioned him|וָאַ֣עַן\rb* \rb further|שֵׁנִ֔ית\rb*\rb |וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑יו\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb are the two|שְׁתֵּ֞י\rb* \rb olive|הַזֵּיתִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb branches|שִׁבֲּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb beside|בְּיַ֗ד\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb pipes|צַנְתְּר֣וֹת\rb* \rb from which|מֵעֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the golden oil|הַזָּהָֽב׃\rb*\f + \fr 4:12 \ft Hebrew \fqa from which the gold\f* \rb pours|הַֽמְרִיקִ֥ים\rb*?”
\p \v 13 “\rb Do you not|הֲל֥וֹא\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֖עְתָּ\rb* \rb what|מָה־\rb* \rb these are|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb*?” \rb he inquired|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַי֙\rb*.
\p “\rb No|לֹ֥א\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb*,” \rb I replied|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb So he said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb These|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb are the two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb anointed|הַיִּצְהָ֑ר\rb* \rb ones|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\f + \fr 4:14 \ft Hebrew \fqa the two sons of new oil\f* \rb who are standing|הָעֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲד֥וֹן\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”\f + \fr 4:14 \ft See \ref Revelation 11:4|REV 11:4\ref*.\f*
\c 5
\s1 The Vision of the Flying Scroll
\p \v 1 \rb Again|וָאָשׁ֕וּב\rb* \rb I lifted up|וָאֶשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינַ֖י\rb* \rb and saw|וָֽאֶרְאֶ֑ה\rb* \rb before me|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb a flying|עָפָֽה׃\rb* \rb scroll|מְגִלָּ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 2 “\rb What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb do you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶ֑ה\rb*?” \rb asked the angel|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb*.
\p “\rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶה֙\rb* \rb a flying|עָפָ֔ה\rb* \rb scroll|מְגִלָּ֣ה\rb*,” \rb I replied|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb long|אָרְכָּהּ֙\rb* \rb and ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|בָּאַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb wide|וְרָחְבָּ֖הּ\rb*.\f + \fr 5:2 \ft The flying scroll was approximately 30 feet long and 15 feet wide (9.1 meters long and 4.6 meters wide).\f*”
\p \v 3 \rb Then he told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb This|זֹ֚את\rb* \rb is the curse|הָֽאָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb that is going out|הַיּוֹצֵ֖את\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb according to|כָּמ֣וֹהָ\rb* \rb one side of the scroll|מִזֶּה֙\rb*, \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb thief|הַגֹּנֵ֗ב\rb* \rb will be removed|נִקָּ֔ה\rb*; \rb and according to|כָּמ֥וֹהָ\rb* \rb the other side|מִזֶּ֖ה\rb*, \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb perjurer|הַנִּ֨שְׁבָּ֔ע\rb* \rb will be removed|נִקָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb I will send it out|הוֹצֵאתִ֗יהָ\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and it will enter|וּבָ֙אָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the thief|הַגַּנָּ֔ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the house|בֵּ֛ית\rb* \rb of him who swears|הַנִּשְׁבָּ֥ע\rb* \rb falsely|לַשָּׁ֑קֶר\rb* \rb by My name|בִּשְׁמִ֖י\rb*. \rb It will remain|וְלָ֙נֶה֙\rb* \rb inside|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb* \rb and destroy it|וְכִלַּ֖תּוּ\rb*, \rb down to|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its timbers|עֵצָ֥יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and stones|אֲבָנָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Vision of the Woman in a Basket
\p \v 5 \rb Then the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֑י\rb* \rb came forward|וַיֵּצֵ֕א\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb Now|נָ֤א\rb* \rb lift up|שָׂ֣א\rb* \rb your eyes|עֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and see|וּרְאֵ֔ה\rb* \rb what|מָ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb is approaching|הַיּוֹצֵ֥את\rb*.”
\p \v 6 “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is it|הִ֑יא\rb*?” \rb I asked|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*.
\p \rb And he replied|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb |זֹ֤את\rb* \rb A measuring basket|הָֽאֵיפָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 5:6 \ft Or \fqa An ephah\f* \rb is going forth|הַיּוֹצֵ֔את\rb*.” \rb Then he continued|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is their iniquity|עֵינָ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 5:6 \ft One Hebrew manuscript, LXX, and Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa their appearance \ft or (literally) \fqa their eye\f* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb And behold|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb*, \rb the cover|כִּכַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of lead|עֹפֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb was raised|נִשֵּׂ֑את\rb*,\rb |וְזֹאת֙\rb* \rb and there was|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb a woman|אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb sitting|יוֹשֶׁ֖בֶת\rb* \rb inside|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the basket|הָאֵיפָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 “\rb This|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb is Wickedness|הָרִשְׁעָ֔ה\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*. \rb And he shoved her down|וַיַּשְׁלֵ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the basket|הָֽאֵיפָ֑ה\rb*, \rb pushing down|וַיַּשְׁלֵ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lead|הָעֹפֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb cover|אֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb its opening|פִּֽיהָ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then I lifted|וָאֶשָּׂ֨א\rb* \rb up my eyes|עֵינַ֜י\rb* \rb and saw|וָאֵ֗רֶא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb two|שְׁתַּ֨יִם\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb approaching|יֽוֹצְאוֹת֙\rb*, \rb with the wind|וְר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb in their wings|בְּכַנְפֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Their|וְלָהֵ֥נָּה\rb* \rb wings|כְנָפַ֖יִם\rb* \rb were like those|כְּכַנְפֵ֣י\rb* \rb of a stork|הַחֲסִידָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and they lifted up|וַתִּשֶּׂ֙אנָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the basket|הָ֣אֵיפָ֔ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*.
\p \v 10 “\rb Where|אָ֛נָה\rb* \rb are they|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb taking|מֽוֹלִכ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the basket|הָאֵיפָֽה׃\rb*?” \rb I asked|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֑י\rb*.
\p \v 11 “\rb To build|לִבְנֽוֹת־\rb* \rb a house|בַ֖יִת\rb* \rb for it|לָ֥הֿ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Shinar|שִׁנְעָ֑ר\rb*,\f + \fr 5:11 \ft That is, Babylonia\f*” \rb he told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*. “\rb And when it is ready|וְהוּכַ֛ן\rb*, \rb the basket will be set|וְהֻנִּ֥יחָה\rb* \rb there|שָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its pedestal|מְכֻנָתָֽהּ׃ס\rb*.”
\c 6
\s1 The Vision of the Four Chariots
\p \v 1 \rb And again|וָאָשֻׁ֗ב\rb* \rb I lifted|וָאֶשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb up my eyes|עֵינַי֙\rb* \rb and saw|וָֽאֶרְאֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb chariots|מַרְכָּבוֹת֙\rb* \rb coming out|יֹֽצְא֔וֹת\rb* \rb from between|מִבֵּ֖ין\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb mountains|הֶֽהָרִ֑ים\rb* — \rb mountains|וְהֶהָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |הָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb The first|הָרִֽאשֹׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb chariot|בַּמֶּרְכָּבָ֥ה\rb* \rb had red|אֲדֻמִּ֑ים\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִ֣ים\rb*, \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖ית\rb*\rb |וּבַמֶּרְכָּבָ֥ה\rb* \rb black|שְׁחֹרִֽים׃\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִ֥ים\rb*, \v 3 \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֖ית\rb*\rb |וּבַמֶּרְכָּבָ֥ה\rb* \rb white|לְבָנִ֑ים\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and the fourth|הָרְבִעִ֔ית\rb*\rb |וּבַמֶּרְכָּבָה֙\rb* \rb dappled|בְּרֻדִּ֖ים\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִ֥ים\rb*— \rb all of them strong|אֲמֻצִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb |וָאַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb So I inquired|וָֽאֹמַ֔ר\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb who was speaking|הַדֹּבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֑י\rb*, “\rb What|מָה־\rb* \rb are these|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 5 \rb And|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb* \rb the angel|הַמַּלְאָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*, “\rb These|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb are the four|אַרְבַּע֙\rb* \rb spirits|רֻח֣וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 6:5 \ft Or \fqa winds\f* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb going forth|יוֹצְא֕וֹת\rb* \rb from their station|מֵֽהִתְיַצֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲד֥וֹן\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb The one|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with|בָּ֞הּ\rb* \rb the black|הַשְּׁחֹרִ֗ים\rb* \rb horses|הַסּוּסִ֣ים\rb* \rb is going|יֹֽצְאִים֙\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the north|צָפ֔וֹן\rb*, \rb the one with the white horses|וְהַלְּבָנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |יָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the west|אַֽחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*,\f + \fr 6:6 \ft Or \fqa the one with the white horses after them\f* \rb and the one with the dappled horses|וְהַ֨בְּרֻדִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |יָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb the south|הַתֵּימָֽן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb As the strong horses|וְהָאֲמֻצִּ֣ים\rb* \rb went out|יָצְא֗וּ\rb*, \rb they were eager|וַיְבַקְשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb to go|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb and patrol|לְהִתְהַלֵּ֣ך\rb* \rb the earth|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*; \rb and the LORD said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go|לְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb and patrol|הִתְהַלְּכ֣וּ\rb* \rb the earth|בָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*.” \rb So they patrolled|וַתִּתְהַלַּ֖כְנָה\rb* \rb the earth|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Then the LORD summoned|וַיַּזְעֵ֣ק\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֔י\rb*\rb |וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Behold|רְאֵ֗ה\rb*, \rb those going|הַיּֽוֹצְאִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the north|צָפ֔וֹן\rb* \rb have given rest|הֵנִ֥יחוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to My Spirit|רוּחִ֖י\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the north|צָפֽוֹן׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 The Crown and the Temple
\p \v 9 \rb The word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb also came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 10 “\rb Take|לָק֙וֹחַ֙\rb* \rb an offering from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the exiles|הַגּוֹלָ֔ה\rb* — \rb from Heldai|מֵחֶלְדַּ֕י\rb*,\rb |וּמֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb Tobijah|טוֹבִיָּ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וּמֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and Jedaiah|יְדַֽעְיָ֑ה\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb have arrived|בָּ֖אוּ\rb* \rb from Babylon|מִבָּבֶֽל׃\rb* — \rb and go|וּבָאתָ֤\rb* \rb that same|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֚ית\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Zephaniah|צְפַנְיָ֔ה\rb*. \v 11 \rb Take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb silver|כֶֽסֶף־\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֖ב\rb*, \rb make|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb an ornate crown|עֲטָר֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and set|וְשַׂמְתָּ֗\rb* \rb it on the head|בְּרֹ֛אשׁ\rb* \rb of the high|הַגָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֥ן\rb*, \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehozadak|יְהוֹצָדָ֖ק\rb*.\f + \fr 6:11 \fqa Jehozadak \ft is a variant of \fqa Jozadak\ft ; see \ref Ezra 3:2|EZR 3:2\ref*.\f*
\p \v 12 \rb And you are to tell him|וְאָמַרְתָּ֤\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb says|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: ‘\rb Here is|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb whose name is|שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb the Branch|צֶ֤מַח\rb*, \rb and He will branch out|יִצְמָ֔ח\rb* \rb from His place|וּמִתַּחְתָּ֣יו\rb* \rb and build|וּבָנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵיכַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Yes, He|וְ֠הוּא\rb* \rb will build|יִבְנֶ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵיכַ֤ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*; \rb He|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb will be clothed in|יִשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb splendor|ה֔וֹד\rb* \rb and will sit|וְיָשַׁ֥ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb His throne|כִּסְא֑וֹ\rb* \rb and rule|וּמָשַׁ֖ל\rb*. \rb And He will be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb a priest|כֹהֵן֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb His throne|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 6:13 \ft Or \fqa And there will be a priest on His throne\f* \rb and there will be|תִּהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb peaceful|שָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb counsel|וַעֲצַ֣ת\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 14 \rb The crown|וְהָעֲטָרֹ֗ת\rb* \rb will reside|תִּֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb in the temple|בְּהֵיכַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb as a memorial|לְזִכָּר֖וֹן\rb* \rb to Helem|לְחֵ֙לֶם֙\rb*,\f + \fr 6:14 \ft Hebrew; Syriac \fqa Heldai\ft ; see verse 10.\f* \rb Tobijah|וּלְטוֹבִיָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb Jedaiah|וְלִידַֽעְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and the gracious|וּלְחֵ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 6:14 \ft Or \fqa and Hen\ft ; Syriac \fqa and Josiah\ft ; see verse 10.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zephaniah|צְפַנְיָ֑ה\rb*. \v 15 \rb Even those far away|וּרְחוֹקִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb will come|יָבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb and build|וּבָנוּ֙\rb* \rb the temple|בְּהֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and you will know|וִידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb has sent Me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb This will happen|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you diligently obey|שָׁמ֣וֹעַ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמְע֔וּן\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\c 7
\s1 A Call to Justice and Mercy
\p \v 1 \rb In the fourth|אַרְבַּ֔ע\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb Darius|לְדָרְיָ֖וֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֗ה\rb* \rb on the fourth|בְּאַרְבָּעָ֛ה\rb* \rb day of the ninth|הַתְּשִׁעִ֖י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the month of Chislev|בְּכִסְלֵֽו׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa Chislev \ft is the ninth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of November and December.\f* \v 2 \rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Now the people of Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb*\rb |שַׂר־\rb* \rb Sharezer|אֶ֕צֶר\rb*\rb |וְרֶ֥גֶם\rb* \rb and Regem-melech|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb along with their men|וַֽאֲנָשָׁ֑יו\rb*,\f + \fr 7:2 \ft Or \fqa Bethel-sharezer had sent Regem-melech, along with his men,\f* \rb to plead|לְחַלּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb by asking|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb of the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb as well as|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Should I weep|הַֽאֶבְכֶּה֙\rb* \rb and fast|הִנָּזֵ֕ר\rb* \rb in the fifth|הַחֲמִשִׁ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb* \rb these|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb many|כַּמֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִֽים׃פ\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 5 “\rb Ask|אֱמֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you fasted|צַמְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb and mourned|וְסָפ֜וֹד\rb* \rb in the fifth|בַּחֲמִישִׁ֣י\rb* \rb and seventh months|וּבַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb for these|וְזֶה֙\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb was it really for Me|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb that you fasted|הֲצ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |צַמְתֻּ֖נִי\rb*? \v 6 \rb And when|וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb you were eating|תֹאכְל֖וּ\rb*\rb |וְכִ֣י\rb* \rb and drinking|תִשְׁתּ֑וּ\rb*, \rb were you not|הֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb doing so|אַתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |הָאֹ֣כְלִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb simply for yourselves|הַשֹּׁתִֽים׃\rb*? \v 7 \rb Are these not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb proclaimed|קָרָ֤א\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb the earlier|הָרִֽאשֹׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֣ים\rb*, \rb when Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb and its surrounding|סְבִיבֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb towns|וְעָרֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb were|בִּהְי֤וֹת\rb* \rb populous|יֹשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb and prosperous|וּשְׁלֵוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and the Negev|וְהַנֶּ֥גֶב\rb* \rb and the foothills|וְהַשְּׁפֵלָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 7:7 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb were inhabited|יֹשֵֽׁב׃פ\rb*?’”
\p \v 8 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֖ה\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 9 “\rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֛ר\rb*: ‘\rb Administer|שְׁפֹ֔טוּ\rb* \rb true|אֱמֶת֙\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפַּ֤ט\rb*. \rb Show|עֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb loving devotion|וְחֶ֣סֶד\rb*\f + \fr 7:9 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb and compassion|וְרַֽחֲמִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb one|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb another|אָחִֽיו׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb oppress|תַּעֲשֹׁ֑קוּ\rb* \rb the widow|וְאַלְמָנָ֧ה\rb* \rb or the fatherless|וְיָת֛וֹם\rb*, \rb the foreigner|גֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb or the poor|וְעָנִ֖י\rb*. \rb And do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb plot|תַּחְשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb evil|וְרָעַת֙\rb* \rb in your hearts|בִּלְבַבְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb against one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another|אָחִ֔יו\rb*.’
\p \v 11 \rb But they refused|וַיְמָאֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb to pay attention|לְהַקְשִׁ֔יב\rb* \rb and turned|וַיִּתְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb a stubborn|סֹרָ֑רֶת\rb* \rb shoulder|כָתֵ֖ף\rb*; \rb they stopped up|הִכְבִּ֥ידוּ\rb* \rb their ears|וְאָזְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from hearing|מִשְּׁמֽוֹעַ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:11 \ft Hebrew \fqa they made their ears too heavy to hear\f* \v 12 \rb They made|שָׂ֣מוּ\rb* \rb their hearts|וְלִבָּ֞ם\rb* \rb like flint|שָׁמִ֗יר\rb* \rb and would not listen to|מִ֠שְּׁמוֹעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the law|הַתּוֹרָ֤ה\rb* \rb or|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb to the words|הַדְּבָרִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb had sent|שָׁלַ֜ח\rb* \rb by His Spirit|בְּרוּח֔וֹ\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb the earlier|הָרִֽאשֹׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֣ים\rb*. \rb Therefore great|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb anger|קֶ֣צֶף\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb just as|כַאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I had called|קָרָ֖א\rb* \rb and they would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמֵ֑עוּ\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb when they called|יִקְרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb I would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen|אֶשְׁמָ֔ע\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb But I scattered them with a whirlwind|וְאֵ֣סָעֲרֵ֗ם\rb* \rb among|עַ֤ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb known|יְדָע֔וּם\rb*, \rb and the land|וְהָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb was left desolate|נָשַׁ֣מָּה\rb* \rb behind them|אַֽחֲרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb so that no one could come|מֵֽעֹבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb or go|וּמִשָּׁ֑ב\rb*. \rb Thus they turned|וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb the pleasant|חֶמְדָּ֖ה\rb* \rb land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb into a desolation|לְשַׁמָּֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 8
\s1 The Restoration of Jerusalem
\r (\ref Micah 4:6–13|MIC 4:6-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Again the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb came to me|וַיְהִ֛י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 2 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: “\rb I am jealous|קִנֵּ֥אתִי\rb* \rb for Zion|לְצִיּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb with great|גְדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb zeal|קִנְאָ֣ה\rb*; \rb I am jealous|קִנֵּ֥אתִי\rb* \rb for her|לָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb with great|גְדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb fervor|וְחֵמָ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: “\rb I will return|שַׁ֚בְתִּי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Zion|צִיּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and dwell|וְשָׁכַנְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb in|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb will be called|וְנִקְרְאָ֤ה\rb* \rb the City|עִ֣יר־\rb* \rb of Truth|הָֽאֱמֶ֔ת\rb*, \rb and the mountain|וְהַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb will be called the Holy|הַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb Mountain|הַ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: “\rb Old men|זְקֵנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and old women|וּזְקֵנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb will again|עֹ֤ד\rb* \rb sit|יֵֽשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb along the streets|בִּרְחֹב֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb each|וְאִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb with a staff|מִשְׁעַנְתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb in hand|בְּיָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb because of|מֵרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb great age|יָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And the streets|וּרְחֹב֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb will be filled|יִמָּ֣לְא֔וּ\rb* \rb with boys|יְלָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb and girls|וִֽילָד֑וֹת\rb* \rb playing|מְשַׂחֲקִ֖ים\rb* \rb there|בִּרְחֹֽבֹתֶֽיהָ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: “\rb If|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is impossible|יִפָּלֵ֗א\rb*\f + \fr 8:6 \ft Or \fqa marvelous\ft ; twice in this verse\f* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵי֙\rb* \rb of the remnant|שְׁאֵרִית֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb in these|הָהֵ֑ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֖ים\rb*, \rb should it also|גַּם־\rb* \rb be impossible|יִפָּלֵ֔א\rb* \rb in My eyes|בְּעֵינַי֙\rb*?” \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: “\rb I will save|מוֹשִׁ֛יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the east|מִזְרָ֑ח\rb* \rb and from the land|וּמֵאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of|מְב֥וֹא\rb* \rb the west|הַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb I will bring them|וְהֵבֵאתִ֣י\rb* \rb back|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb to dwell|וְשָׁכְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb where they will be|וְהָיוּ־\rb* \rb My|לִ֣י\rb* \rb people|לְעָ֗ם\rb*, \rb and I|וַֽאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will be|אֶהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb faithful|בֶּאֱמֶ֖ת\rb* \rb and righteous|וּבִצְדָקָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb God|לֵֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: “\rb Let your hands|יְדֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb be strong|תֶּחֱזַ֣קְנָה\rb*, \rb you who now|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb hear|הַשֹּֽׁמְעִים֙\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb spoken|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb*\rb |מִפִּי֙\rb* \rb by the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb* \rb who were present when|בְּי֞וֹם\rb* \rb the foundations were laid|יֻסַּ֨ד\rb* \rb to rebuild|לְהִבָּנֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb the temple|הַהֵיכָ֖ל\rb*, \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֛וֹת\rb*. \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb neither|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb nor|אֵינֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb beast|הַבְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb received|נִֽהְיָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וּשְׂכַ֥ר\rb* \rb wages|שְׂכַ֤ר\rb*, \rb nor was there|אֵין־\rb* \rb safety|שָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the enemy|הַצָּ֔ר\rb* \rb for anyone who came|וְלַיּוֹצֵ֨א\rb* \rb or went|וְלַבָּ֤א\rb*, \rb for I had turned|וַאֲשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb against his neighbor|בְּרֵעֵֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb will not treat|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb the remnant|לִשְׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb as I did in the past|הָרִֽאשֹׁנִים֙\rb*\rb |כַיָּמִ֤ים\rb*,” \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 “\rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the seed|זֶ֣רַע\rb* \rb will be prosperous|הַשָּׁל֗וֹם\rb*, \rb the vine|הַגֶּ֜פֶן\rb* \rb will yield|תִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb its fruit|פִּרְיָהּ֙\rb*, \rb the ground|וְהָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb will yield|תִּתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its produce|יְבוּלָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and the skies|וְהַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will give|יִתְּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb their dew|טַלָּ֑ם\rb*. \rb To the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֛ית\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb I will give all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these things|אֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb as an inheritance|וְהִנְחַלְתִּ֗י\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 13 \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb you have been|הֱיִיתֶ֨ם\rb* \rb a curse|קְלָלָ֜ה\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and house|וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb I will save|אוֹשִׁ֣יעַ\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and you will be|וִהְיִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a blessing|בְּרָכָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֖אוּ\rb*; \rb let your hands|יְדֵיכֶֽם׃ס\rb* \rb be strong|תֶּחֱזַ֥קְנָה\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: “\rb Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I resolved|זָמַמְ֜תִּי\rb* \rb to bring disaster|לְהָרַ֣ע\rb* \rb upon you|לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb when your fathers|אֲבֹֽתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb provoked Me to anger|בְּהַקְצִ֤יף\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֔י\rb*, \rb and I did not|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb relent|נִחָֽמְתִּי׃\rb*,” \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb*, \v 15 “\rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb now|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb I have resolved|זָמַ֙מְתִּי֙\rb* \rb to do good|לְהֵיטִ֥יב\rb* \rb again|שַׁ֤בְתִּי\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָֽאוּ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb These|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb are the things|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you must do|תַּֽעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*: \rb Speak|דַּבְּר֤וּ\rb* \rb truth|אֱמֶת֙\rb* \rb to one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb another|רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb render true|אֱמֶת֙\rb* \rb and sound|שָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb judgments|וּמִשְׁפַּ֣ט\rb*\rb |שִׁפְט֖וּ\rb* \rb in your gates|בְּשַׁעֲרֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb |וְאִ֣ישׁ׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb plot|תַּחְשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb evil|רָעַ֣ת\rb* \rb in your hearts|בִּלְבַבְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb against your neighbor|רֵעֵ֗הוּ\rb*, \rb and do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb love|תֶּאֱהָ֑בוּ\rb* \rb to swear|וּשְׁבֻ֥עַת\rb* \rb falsely|שֶׁ֖קֶר\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I hate|שָׂנֵ֖אתִי\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֛לֶּה\rb*,”\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 19 “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*: \rb The fasts|צ֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֡י\rb*,\rb |וְצ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁי֩\rb*,\rb |וְצ֨וֹם\rb* \rb the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֜י\rb*, \rb and|וְצ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the tenth months|הָעֲשִׂירִ֗י\rb* \rb will become|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb times of joy|לְשָׂשׂ֣וֹן\rb* \rb and gladness|וּלְשִׂמְחָ֔ה\rb*, \rb cheerful|טוֹבִ֑ים\rb* \rb feasts|וּֽלְמֹעֲדִ֖ים\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*. \rb Therefore you are to love|אֱהָֽבוּ׃פ\rb* \rb both truth|וְהָאֱמֶ֥ת\rb* \rb and peace|וְהַשָּׁל֖וֹם\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: “\rb Peoples|עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb will yet|עֹ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb come|יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb* — \rb the residents|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of many|רַבּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb* — \v 21 \rb and the residents|יֹשְׁבֵי֩\rb* \rb of one|אַחַ֨ת\rb* \rb city will go|וְֽהָלְכ֡וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb another|אַחַ֜ת\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*: ‘\rb Let us go|נֵלְכָ֤ה\rb*\rb |הָלוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb at once to plead|לְחַלּוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and to seek|וּלְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb*. \rb I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb myself|גַּם־\rb* \rb am going|אֵלְכָ֖ה\rb*.’ \v 22 \rb And many|רַבִּים֙\rb* \rb peoples|עַמִּ֤ים\rb* \rb and strong|עֲצוּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb nations|וְגוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb will come|וּבָ֨אוּ\rb* \rb to seek|לְבַקֵּ֛שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and to plead|וּלְחַלּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: “\rb In those|הָהֵ֔מָּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb from the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb* \rb of every|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb tongue|לְשֹׁנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb will tightly|יַחֲזִ֙יקוּ֙\rb* \rb grasp|וְֽהֶחֱזִ֡יקוּ\rb* \rb the robe|בִּכְנַף֩\rb* \rb of a Jew|יְהוּדִ֜י\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Let us go|נֵֽלְכָה֙\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we have heard|שָׁמַ֖עְנוּ\rb* \rb that God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb is with you|עִמָּכֶֽם׃ס\rb*.’”
\c 9
\s1 The Burden against Israel’s Enemies
\q1 \v 1 \rb This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb of the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb against the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Hadrach|חַדְרָ֔ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and Damascus|וְדַמֶּ֖שֶׂק\rb* \rb its resting place|מְנֻחָת֑וֹ\rb*—
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the eyes|עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of men|אָדָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and of all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\q2 \rb are upon the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 9:1 \ft Or \fqa for the eye of the LORD is on all men and all the tribes of Israel\f*—
\q1 \v 2 \rb and also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb against Hamath|חֲמָ֖ת\rb*,
\q2 \rb which borders|תִּגְבָּל־\rb* \rb it|בָּ֑הּ\rb*,
\q1 \rb as well as Tyre|צֹ֣ר\rb* \rb and Sidon|וְצִיד֔וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb though|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they are very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb shrewd|חָֽכְמָ֖ה\rb*.
\b 
