\q2 \rb will live|וְחָי֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and return|וָשָֽׁבוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb I will bring them back|וַהֲשִֽׁיבוֹתִים֙\rb* \rb from|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and gather them|אֲקַבְּצֵ֑ם\rb* \rb from Assyria|וּמֵֽאַשּׁ֖וּר\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will bring|אֲבִיאֵ֔ם\rb* \rb them|וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb to Gilead|גִּלְעָ֤ד\rb* \rb and Lebanon|וּלְבָנוֹן֙\rb*
\q2 \rb until no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb more room is found|יִמָּצֵ֖א\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb They will pass|וְעָבַ֨ר\rb* \rb through the sea|בַּיָּ֜ם\rb* \rb of distress|צָרָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and strike|וְהִכָּ֤ה\rb* \rb the waves|גַּלִּ֔ים\rb* \rb of the sea|בַיָּם֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the depths|מְצוּל֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the Nile|יְאֹ֑ר\rb* \rb will dry up|וְהֹבִ֕ישׁוּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb The pride|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb will be brought down|וְהוּרַד֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the scepter|וְשֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will depart|יָסֽוּר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb I will strengthen them|וְגִבַּרְתִּים֙\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and in His name|וּבִשְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb they will walk|יִתְהַלָּ֑כוּ\rb*,”
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\c 11
\s1 The Doomed Flock
\q1 \v 1 \rb Open|פְּתַ֥ח\rb* \rb your doors|דְּלָתֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb O Lebanon|לְבָנ֖וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb that the fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb may consume|וְתֹאכַ֥ל\rb* \rb your cedars|בַּאֲרָזֶֽיךָ׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 2 \rb Wail|הֵילֵ֤ל\rb*, \rb O cypress|בְּרוֹשׁ֙\rb*,\f + \fr 11:2 \ft Or \fqa pine \ft or \fqa juniper \ft or \fqa fir\f* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the cedar|אֶ֔רֶז\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb has fallen|נָ֣פַל\rb*;
\q2 \rb the majestic trees|אַדִּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb are ruined|שֻׁדָּ֑דוּ\rb*!
\q1 \rb Wail|הֵילִ֙ילוּ֙\rb*, \rb O oaks|אַלּוֹנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Bashan|בָשָׁ֔ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the dense|הַבָּצוּר׃\rb* \rb forest|יַ֥עַר\rb* \rb has been cut down|יָרַ֖ד\rb*!
\q1 \v 3 \rb Listen to|ק֚וֹל\rb* \rb the wailing|יִֽלְלַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the shepherds|הָרֹעִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb their glory|אַדַּרְתָּ֑ם\rb*\rb |ק֚וֹל\rb* \rb is in ruins|שֻׁדְּדָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb Listen to the roaring|שַׁאֲגַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the young lions|כְּפִירִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the thickets|גְּא֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃ס\rb* \rb are destroyed|שֻׁדַּ֖ד\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: “\rb Pasture|רְעֵ֖ה\rb* \rb the flock|צֹ֥אן\rb* \rb marked for slaughter|הַהֲרֵגָֽה׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb buyers|קֹנֵיהֶ֤ן\rb* \rb slaughter them|יַֽהֲרְגֻן֙\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb remorse|יֶאְשָׁ֔מוּ\rb*. \rb Those who sell them|וּמֹכְרֵיהֶ֣ן\rb* \rb say|יֹאמַ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Blessed be|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb for I am rich|וַאעְשִׁ֑ר\rb*!’ \rb Even their own shepherds|וְרֹ֣עֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb have no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb compassion|יַחְמ֖וֹל\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb I will no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb have compassion|אֶחְמ֥וֹל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb but behold|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb will cause each|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb to fall|מַמְצִ֣יא\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of his neighbor|רֵעֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb and|וּבְיַ֣ד\rb* \rb his king|מַלְכּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb who will devastate|וְכִתְּתוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb and I will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb deliver it|אַצִּ֖יל\rb* \rb from their hands|מִיָּדָֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb So I pastured|וָֽאֶרְעֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the flock|צֹ֣אן\rb* \rb marked for slaughter|הַֽהֲרֵגָ֔ה\rb*, \rb especially|לָכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb the afflicted|עֲנִיֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the flock|הַצֹּ֑אן\rb*. \rb Then I took|וָאֶקַּֽח־\rb* \rb for myself|לִ֞י\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb staffs|מַקְל֗וֹת\rb*, \rb calling|קָרָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb one|לְאַחַ֞ד\rb* \rb Favor|נֹ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb and the other|וּלְאַחַד֙\rb*\rb |קָרָ֣אתִי\rb* \rb Union|חֹֽבְלִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and I pastured|וָאֶרְעֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּֽאן׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb And in one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb month|בְּיֶ֣רַח\rb* \rb I dismissed|וָאַכְחִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb shepherds|הָרֹעִ֖ים\rb*.
\p \rb My soul|נַפְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb grew impatient|וַתִּקְצַ֤ר\rb* \rb with the flock|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and their souls|נַפְשָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb detested|בָּחֲלָ֥ה\rb* \rb me|בִֽי׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Then I said|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb I will no longer|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb shepherd you|אֶרְעֶ֖ה\rb*.\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Let the dying|הַמֵּתָ֣ה\rb* \rb die|תָמ֗וּת\rb*, \rb and the perishing|וְהַנִּכְחֶ֙דֶת֙\rb* \rb perish|תִּכָּחֵ֔ד\rb*; \rb and let those who remain|וְהַ֨נִּשְׁאָר֔וֹת\rb* \rb devour|תֹּאכַ֕לְנָה\rb* \rb one|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb another’s|רְעוּתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb flesh|בְּשַׂ֥ר\rb*.”
\s1 Thirty Pieces of Silver
\r (\ref Matthew 27:3–10|MAT 27:3-10\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb Next I took|וָאֶקַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my staff|מַקְלִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb called Favor|נֹ֔עַם\rb* \rb and cut it in two|וָאֶגְדַּ֖ע\rb*,\f + \fr 11:10 \ft Or \fqa broke it\ft ; similarly in verse 14\f*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb revoking|לְהָפֵיר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִיתִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had made|כָּרַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הָעַמִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb It was revoked|וַתֻּפַ֖ר\rb* \rb on that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb and so|כֵ֜ן\rb* \rb the afflicted|עֲנִיֵּ֤י\rb* \rb of the flock|הַצֹּאן֙\rb* \rb who were watching|הַשֹּׁמְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֔י\rb* \rb knew|וַיֵּדְע֨וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb was the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Then I told|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb it seems|בְּעֵינֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb right to you|ט֧וֹב\rb*, \rb give me|הָב֥וּ\rb* \rb my wages|שְׂכָרִ֖י\rb*; \rb but if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א׀\rb*, \rb keep them|חֲדָ֑לוּ\rb*.” \rb So they weighed out|וַיִּשְׁקְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my wages|שְׂכָרִ֖י\rb*, \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb pieces of silver|כָּֽסֶף׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֶל־\rb*, “\rb Throw|הַשְׁלִיכֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb it to|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb the potter|הַיּוֹצֵ֔ר\rb*”— \rb this magnificent|אֶ֣דֶר\rb* \rb price|הַיְקָ֔ר\rb* \rb at which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they valued me|יָקַ֖רְתִּי\rb*\rb |מֵֽעֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb So I took|וָֽאֶקְחָה֙\rb* \rb the thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb pieces of silver|הַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb and threw|וָאַשְׁלִ֥יךְ\rb* \rb them|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the potter|הַיּוֹצֵֽר׃\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Then I cut in two|וָֽאֶגְדַּע֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb staff|מַקְלִ֣י\rb* \rb called Union|הַחֹֽבְלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb breaking|לְהָפֵר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the brotherhood|הָֽאַחֲוָ֔ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*: “\rb Take up|קַח־\rb* \rb once more|ע֣וֹד\rb* \rb the equipment|כְּלִ֖י\rb* \rb of a foolish|אֱוִלִֽי׃\rb* \rb shepherd|רֹעֶ֥ה\rb*. \v 16 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb behold|הִנֵּֽה־\rb*, \rb I|אָנֹכִי֩\rb* \rb will raise up|מֵקִ֨ים\rb* \rb a shepherd|רֹעֶ֜ה\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb who will neither|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb care for|יִפְקֹד֙\rb* \rb the lost|הַנִּכְחָד֤וֹת\rb*, \rb nor|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb seek|יְבַקֵּ֔שׁ\rb* \rb the young|הַנַּ֣עַר\rb*, \rb nor heal|יְרַפֵּ֑א\rb* \rb the broken|וְהַנִּשְׁבֶּ֖רֶת\rb*, \rb nor|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb sustain|יְכַלְכֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb the healthy|הַנִּצָּבָה֙\rb*,\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb but he will devour|יֹאכַ֔ל\rb* \rb the flesh|וּבְשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of the choice sheep|הַבְּרִיאָה֙\rb* \rb and tear off|יְפָרֵֽק׃ס\rb* \rb their hooves|וּפַרְסֵיהֶ֖ן\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb Woe|ה֣וֹי\rb* \rb to the worthless|הָֽאֱלִיל֙\rb* \rb shepherd|רֹעִ֤י\rb*,
\q2 \rb who deserts|עֹזְבִ֣י\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb*!
\q1 \rb May a sword|חֶ֥רֶב\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb strike his arm|זְרוֹע֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb*
\q2 \rb and his right|יְמִינ֑וֹ\rb* \rb eye|עֵ֣ין\rb*!
\q1 \rb May his arm|זְרֹעוֹ֙\rb* \rb be completely withered|יָב֣וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |תִּיבָ֔שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb and his right|יְמִינ֖וֹ\rb* \rb eye|וְעֵ֥ין\rb* \rb utterly blinded|כָּהֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |תִכְהֶֽה׃ס\rb*!”
\c 12
\s1 The Coming Deliverance of Jerusalem
\d \v 1 \rb This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb of the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.
\p \rb Thus declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb who stretches out|נֹטֶ֤ה\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and lays the foundation|וְיֹסֵ֣ד\rb* \rb of the earth|אָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb who forms|וְיֹצֵ֥ר\rb* \rb the spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb within him|בְּקִרְבּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*:
\p \v 2 “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb I|אָ֠נֹכִי\rb* \rb will make|שָׂ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֧ם\rb* \rb a cup|סַף־\rb* \rb of drunkenness|רַ֛עַל\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the surrounding|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb peoples|הָעַמִּ֖ים\rb*.\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb besieged|בַמָּצ֖וֹר\rb*, \rb as well as|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb |וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb On that|הַ֠הוּא\rb* \rb day|בַיּוֹם־\rb*, \rb when all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb gather|וְנֶאֶסְפ֣וּ\rb* \rb against her|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb I will make|אָשִׂ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb* \rb a heavy|מַֽעֲמָסָה֙\rb* \rb stone|אֶ֤בֶן\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb*; \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who would heave it away|עֹמְסֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb will be severely injured|שָׂר֣וֹט\rb*\rb |יִשָּׂרֵ֑טוּ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb On that|הַה֜וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֨וֹם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb I will strike|אַכֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb every|כָל־\rb* \rb horse|סוּס֙\rb* \rb with panic|בַּתִּמָּה֔וֹן\rb*, \rb and every rider|וְרֹכְב֖וֹ\rb* \rb with madness|בַּשִּׁגָּע֑וֹן\rb*. \rb I will keep a watchful|אֶפְקַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb eye|עֵינַ֔י\rb* \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*, \rb but I will strike|אַכֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb with blindness|בַּֽעִוָּרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the horses|ס֣וּס\rb* \rb of the nations|הָֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then the leaders|אַלֻּפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb will say|וְאָֽמְר֛וּ\rb* \rb in their hearts|בְּלִבָּ֑ם\rb*: ‘\rb The people|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb are my strength|אַמְצָ֥ה\rb*, \rb for the LORD|בַּיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb is their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 6 \rb On that|הַה֡וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will make|אָשִׂים֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the clans|אַלֻּפֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb like a firepot|כְּֽכִיּ֧וֹר\rb*\rb |אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb in a woodpile|בְּעֵצִ֗ים\rb*, \rb like a flaming|אֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb torch|וּכְלַפִּ֥יד\rb* \rb among the sheaves|בְּעָמִ֔יר\rb*; \rb they will consume|וְאָ֨כְל֜וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָעַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb around them|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the right|יָמִ֧ין\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the left|שְׂמֹ֛אול\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb while the people|וְיָשְׁבָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֥ם\rb* \rb remain|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb secure|תַּחְתֶּ֖יהָ\rb* \rb there|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will save|וְהוֹשִׁ֧יעַ\rb* \rb the tents|אָהֳלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb first|בָּרִֽאשֹׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb the glory|תִּפְאֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֗יד\rb* \rb and|וְתִפְאֶ֛רֶת\rb* \rb of the people|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb may not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be greater|תִגְדַּ֜ל\rb* \rb than|עַל־\rb* \rb that of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |בְּעַד֙\rb* \rb will defend|יָגֵ֤ן\rb* \rb the people|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that|הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the weakest|הַנִּכְשָׁ֥ל\rb* \rb among them|בָּהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb like David|כְּדָוִ֑יד\rb*, \rb and the house|וּבֵ֤ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִיד֙\rb* \rb will be like God|כֵּֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb like the angel|כְּמַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 12:8 \ft Or \fqa Angel\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb going before them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb So|וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb on that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will set out|אֲבַקֵּ֗שׁ\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַשְׁמִיד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb that come|הַבָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 Mourning the One They Pierced
\r (\ref John 19:31–37|JHN 19:31-37\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb Then I will pour out|וְשָׁפַכְתִּי֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֜יד\rb* \rb and on|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the people|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb a spirit|ר֤וּחַ\rb*\f + \fr 12:10 \ft Or \fqa the Spirit\f* \rb of grace|חֵן֙\rb* \rb and prayer|וְתַ֣חֲנוּנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and they will look|וְהִבִּ֥יטוּ\rb* \rb on Me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*,\f + \fr 12:10 \ft Or \fqa to Me\f*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the One|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they have pierced|דָּקָ֑רוּ\rb*.\f + \fr 12:10 \ft Cited in \ref John 19:37|JHN 19:37\ref*\f* \rb They will mourn|וְסָפְד֣וּ\rb* \rb for Him|עָלָ֗יו\rb* \rb as one mourns|כְּמִסְפֵּד֙\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb an only child|הַיָּחִ֔יד\rb*, \rb and grieve bitterly|וְהָמֵ֥ר\rb* \rb for Him|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb as one grieves|כְּהָמֵ֥ר\rb* \rb for|עַֽל־\rb* \rb a firstborn son|הַבְּכֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the wailing|הַמִּסְפֵּד֙\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb will be as great|יִגְדַּ֤ל\rb* \rb as the wailing|כְּמִסְפַּ֥ד\rb*\rb |הֲדַדְ־\rb* \rb of Hadad-rimmon|רִמּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb in the plain|בְּבִקְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Megiddo|מְגִדּֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb The land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb will mourn|וְסָפְדָ֣ה\rb*, \rb each|מִשְׁפָּח֥וֹת\rb* \rb clan|מִשְׁפָּח֖וֹת\rb* \rb on its own|לְבָ֑ד\rb*: \rb the clan|מִשְׁפַּ֨חַת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֤יד\rb* \rb and their wives|וּנְשֵׁיהֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |לְבָ֔ד\rb*\rb |לְבָד֙\rb*, \rb the clan|מִשְׁפַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Nathan|נָתָן֙\rb*\rb |לְבָ֔ד\rb* \rb and their wives|וּנְשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְבָֽד׃\rb*, \v 13 \rb the clan|מִשְׁפַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִי֙\rb*\rb |לְבָ֔ד\rb* \rb and their wives|וּנְשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְבָ֑ד\rb*, \rb the clan|מִשְׁפַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb of Shimei|הַשִּׁמְעִי֙\rb*\rb |לְבָ֔ד\rb* \rb and their wives|וּנְשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְבָֽד׃\rb*, \v 14 \rb and all|כֹּ֗ל\rb* \rb the remaining|הַנִּשְׁאָר֔וֹת\rb* \rb clans|הַמִּשְׁפָּחוֹת֙\rb*\rb |מִשְׁפָּחֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |מִשְׁפָּחֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |לְבָ֑ד\rb* \rb and their wives|וּנְשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְבָֽד׃ס\rb*.[’’]
\c 13
\s1 An End to Idolatry
\p \v 1 “\rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb a fountain|מָק֣וֹר\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb opened|נִפְתָּ֔ח\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֖יד\rb* \rb and the people|וּלְיֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb to cleanse them from sin|לְחַטַּ֖את\rb* \rb and impurity|וּלְנִדָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And|וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb on that|הַה֜וּא\rb* \rb day|בַיּ֨וֹם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֣ם׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb*, \rb I will erase|אַכְרִ֞ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the names|שְׁמ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the idols|הָֽעֲצַבִּים֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb and they will no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb longer|ע֑וֹד\rb*\rb |וְגַ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb be remembered|יִזָּכְר֖וּ\rb*. \rb I will also remove|אַעֲבִ֥יר\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֛ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of impurity|הַטֻּמְאָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 13:2 \ft Or \fqa the unclean spirit\f* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb And|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb anyone|אִישׁ֮\rb* \rb still|עוֹד֒\rb* \rb prophesies|יִנָּבֵ֣א\rb*, \rb his father|אָבִ֨יו\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb who bore him|יֹֽלְדָיו֙\rb* \rb will say|וְאָמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵ֠לָיו\rb*, ‘\rb You shall not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb remain alive|תִֽחְיֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you have spoken|דִּבַּ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb falsely|שֶׁ֥קֶר\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.’ \rb When he prophesies|בְּהִנָּבְאֽוֹ׃\rb*, \rb his father|אָבִ֧יהוּ\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb who bore him|יֹלְדָ֖יו\rb* \rb will pierce him through|וּדְקָרֻ֜הוּ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb And|וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb on that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb every|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb prophet|הַנְּבִיאִ֛ים\rb* \rb who prophesies|בְּהִנָּֽבְאֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb will be ashamed|יֵבֹ֧שׁוּ\rb* \rb of his vision|מֵחֶזְיֹנ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and he will not|וְלֹ֧א\rb* \rb put on|יִלְבְּשׁ֛וּ\rb* \rb a hairy|שֵׂעָ֖ר\rb* \rb cloak|אַדֶּ֥רֶת\rb* \rb in order to|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb deceive|כַּחֵֽשׁ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb He will say|וְאָמַ֕ר\rb*, ‘\rb I|אָנֹ֑כִי\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb am not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִ֖יא\rb*; \rb I|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb* \rb work|עֹבֵ֤ד\rb* \rb the land|אֲדָמָה֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb I was purchased as a servant|הִקְנַ֥נִי\rb* \rb in my youth|מִנְּעוּרָֽי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 13:5 \ft Or \fqa I am a farmer, for the land has been my livelihood since my youth.\f*’ \v 6 \rb If someone asks|וְאָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, ‘\rb What|מָ֧ה\rb* \rb are these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb wounds|הַמַּכּ֛וֹת\rb* \rb on your chest|בֵּ֣ין\rb*\rb |יָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*\f + \fr 13:6 \ft Literally \fqa between your hands\f*?’ \rb he will answer|וְאָמַ֕ר\rb*, ‘\rb These are|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the wounds I received|הֻכֵּ֖יתִי\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of my friends|מְאַהֲבָֽי׃ס\rb*.’
\s1 The Shepherd Struck, the Sheep Scattered
\r (\ref Matthew 26:31–35|MAT 26:31-35\ref*; \ref Mark 14:27–31|MRK 14:27-31\ref*)
\q1 \v 7 \rb Awake|עוּרִ֤י\rb*, \rb O sword|חֶ֗רֶב\rb*, \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb My Shepherd|רֹעִי֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb against|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the man|גֶּ֣בֶר\rb* \rb who is My Companion|עֲמִיתִ֔י\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb*.
\q1 \rb Strike|הַ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Shepherd|הָֽרֹעֶה֙\rb*, \rb and the sheep|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb* \rb will be scattered|וּתְפוּצֶ֣יןָ\rb*,\f + \fr 13:7 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 26:31|MAT 26:31\ref* and Mark 14:27\f*
\q2 \rb and I will turn|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the little ones|הַצֹּעֲרִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb And|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb in all|בְכָל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb two-thirds|פִּֽי־\rb*\rb |שְׁנַ֣יִם\rb* \rb will be cut off|יִכָּרְת֖וּ\rb* \rb and perish|יִגְוָ֑עוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but a third|וְהַשְּׁלִשִׁ֖ית\rb* \rb will be left|יִוָּ֥תֶר\rb* \rb in it|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb This third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁית֙\rb* \rb I will bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֤י\rb* \rb through the fire|בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will refine them|וּצְרַפְתִּים֙\rb* \rb like silver|הַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb*\rb |כִּצְרֹ֣ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb and test them|וּבְחַנְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb like gold|הַזָּהָ֑ב\rb*\rb |כִּבְחֹ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.
\q1 \rb They will call|יִקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb on My name|בִשְׁמִ֗י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I|וַֽאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will answer them|אֶעֱנֶ֣ה\rb*.\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb I will say|אָמַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb*, ‘\rb They are My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb*,’
\q2 \rb and they|ה֔וּא\rb*\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb will say|יֹאמַ֖ר\rb*, ‘\rb The LORD is|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃ס\rb*.’”
\c 14
\s1 The Destroyers of Jerusalem Destroyed
\p \v 1 \rb Behold|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb a day|יֽוֹם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is coming|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb when your plunder|שְׁלָלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb will be divided|וְחֻלַּ֥ק\rb* \rb in your presence|בְּקִרְבֵּֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb For I will gather|וְאָסַפְתִּ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם׀\rb* \rb for battle|לַמִּלְחָמָה֒\rb* \rb against|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַם֮\rb*, \rb and the city|הָעִ֗יר\rb* \rb will be captured|וְנִלְכְּדָ֣ה\rb*, \rb the houses|הַבָּ֣תִּ֔ים\rb* \rb looted|וְנָשַׁ֙סּוּ֙\rb*, \rb and the women|וְהַנָּשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb ravished|תִּשָּׁגַלְנָה\rb*. \rb Half|חֲצִ֤י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb will go|וְיָצָ֞א\rb* \rb into exile|בַּגּוֹלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but the rest|וְיֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be removed|יִכָּרֵ֖ת\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will go out|וְיָצָ֣א\rb* \rb to fight|וְנִלְחַ֖ם\rb* \rb against those|הָהֵ֑ם\rb* \rb nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb*, \rb as He fights|הִֽלָּחֲמ֖ו\rb* \rb in the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb*\rb |כְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of battle|קְרָֽב׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb On that|הַ֠הוּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּוֹם־\rb* \rb His feet|רַגְלָ֣יו\rb* \rb will stand|וְעָמְד֣וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the Mount|הַ֨ר\rb* \rb of Olives|הַזֵּתִ֜ים\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb east|מִקֶּדֶם֒\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַם֮\rb*, \rb and the Mount|הַ֨ר\rb* \rb of Olives|הַזֵּיתִ֤ים\rb* \rb will be split|וְנִבְקַע֩\rb* \rb in two|מֵֽחֶצְיוֹ֙\rb* \rb from east|מִזְרָ֣חָה\rb* \rb to west|וָיָ֔מָּה\rb*, \rb forming a great|גְּדוֹלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb valley|גֵּ֖יא\rb*, \rb with half|חֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb the mountain|הָהָ֛ר\rb* \rb moving|וּמָ֨שׁ\rb* \rb to the north|צָפ֖וֹנָה\rb* \rb and half|וְחֶצְיוֹ־\rb* \rb to the south|נֶֽגְבָּה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb You will flee|וְנַסְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb by My mountain|הָרַ֗י\rb* \rb valley|גֵּֽיא־\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it|גֵּי־\rb*\rb |הָרִים֮\rb* \rb will extend|יַגִּ֣יעַ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Azal|אָצַל֒\rb*. \rb You will flee|וְנַסְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you fled|נַסְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the earthquake|הָרַ֔עַשׁ\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֔י\rb* \rb will come|וּבָא֙\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the holy ones|קְדֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb with Him|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 14:5 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa with You\f*
\p \v 6 \rb |וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb On that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb there will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb light|א֔וֹר\rb*, \rb no cold|יְקָר֖וֹת\rb* \rb or frost|יִקְפְּאוּן׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb It will be|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb a unique day|יוֹם־\rb* \rb known|יִוָּדַ֥ע\rb* \rb only|אֶחָ֗ד\rb*\rb |ה֛וּא\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb without|לֹא־\rb* \rb day|י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb or night|לָ֑יְלָה\rb*; \rb but when evening|עֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb comes|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb*, \rb there will be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְעֵֽת־\rb* \rb light|אֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And|וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb on that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb living|חַיִּים֙\rb* \rb water|מַֽיִם־\rb* \rb will flow out|יֵצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb half|חֶצְיָ֗ם\rb* \rb of it toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Eastern|הַקַּדְמוֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּם֙\rb*\f + \fr 14:8 \ft That is, the Dead Sea\f* \rb and the other half|וְחֶצְיָ֖ם\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Western|הָאַחֲר֑וֹן\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֣ם\rb*,\f + \fr 14:8 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea\f* \rb in summer|בַּקַּ֥יִץ\rb* \rb and winter alike|וּבָחֹ֖רֶף\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֧ה\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will become|וְהָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb King|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*— \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb alone|אֶחָ֖ד\rb*, \rb and His name|וּשְׁמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb alone|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb from Geba|מִגֶּ֣בַע\rb* \rb to Rimmon|לְרִמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb south|נֶ֖גֶב\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb will be turned|יִסּ֨וֹב\rb* \rb into a plain|כָּעֲרָבָה֙\rb*, \rb but Jerusalem will be raised up|וְֽרָאֲמָה֩\rb* \rb and will remain|וְיָשְׁבָ֨ה\rb* \rb in her place|תַחְתֶּ֜יהָ\rb*, \rb from the Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֗ן\rb* \rb Gate|לְמִשַּׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the site|מְק֞וֹם\rb* \rb of the First|הָֽרִאשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Corner|הַפִּנִּ֔ים\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*, \rb and from the Tower|וּמִגְדַּ֣ל\rb* \rb of Hananel|חֲנַנְאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb winepresses|יִקְבֵ֥י\rb*. \v 11 \rb People will live|וְיָ֣שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb there|בָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb again|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb will there be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb an utter destruction|וְחֵ֖רֶם\rb*. \rb So Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb will dwell|וְיָשְׁבָ֥ה\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶֽטַח׃\rb*.
\b 
\p \v 12 \rb And this|וְזֹ֣את׀\rb* \rb will be|תִּֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the plague|הַמַּגֵּפָ֗ה\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb strikes|יִגֹּ֤ף\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb have warred|צָבְא֖וּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*: \rb Their flesh|בְּשָׂר֗וֹ\rb* \rb will rot|הָמֵ֣ק׀\rb* \rb while they|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb stand|עֹמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their feet|רַגְלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb their eyes|וְעֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb will rot|תִּמַּ֣קְנָה\rb* \rb in their sockets|בְחֹֽרֵיהֶ֔ן\rb*, \rb and their tongues|וּלְשׁוֹנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb will rot|תִּמַּ֥ק\rb* \rb in their mouths|בְּפִיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb On that|הַה֔וּא\rb*\rb |תִּֽהְיֶ֧ה\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb a great|רַבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb panic|מְהֽוּמַת־\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will come|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb upon them|בָּהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that each|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb will seize|וְהֶחֱזִ֗יקוּ\rb* \rb the hand|יַ֣ד\rb* \rb of another|רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and the hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb of one will rise|וְעָלְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb*\rb |יַ֥ד\rb* \rb the other|רֵעֵֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb will also|וְגַ֨ם־\rb* \rb fight|תִּלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb at Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the wealth|חֵ֨יל\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the surrounding|סָבִ֗יב\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֜ם\rb* \rb will be collected|וְאֻסַּף֩\rb* — \rb gold|זָהָ֥ב\rb*, \rb silver|וָכֶ֛סֶף\rb*, \rb and apparel|וּבְגָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb in great abundance|לָרֹ֥ב\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And a similar|וְכֵ֨ן\rb* \rb plague|מַגֵּפַ֣ת\rb* \rb will strike|תִּֽהְיֶ֜ה\rb* \rb the horses|הַסּ֗וּס\rb* \rb and mules|הַפֶּ֙רֶד֙\rb*, \rb camels|הַגָּמָ֣ל\rb* \rb and donkeys|וְהַחֲמ֔וֹר\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָ֨ל־\rb* \rb the animals|הַבְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in those|הָהֵ֑מָּה\rb* \rb camps|בַּמַּחֲנ֣וֹת\rb*.\rb |כַּמַּגֵּפָ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb*
\s1 All Nations Will Worship the King
\r (\ref Leviticus 23:33–44|LEV 23:33-44\ref*; \ref Nehemiah 8:13–18|NEH 8:13-18\ref*)
\p \v 16 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the survivors|הַנּוֹתָר֙\rb* \rb from|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb that came|הַבָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb will go up|וְעָל֞וּ\rb*\rb |מִדֵּ֧י\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb after year|בְשָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb to worship|לְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֺת֙\rb* \rb the King|לְמֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and to celebrate|וְלָחֹ֖ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Tabernacles|הַסֻּכּֽוֹת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 14:16 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as \fqa the Feast of Booths \ft or \fqa the Feast of Shelters \ft and originally called \fqa the Feast of Ingathering\ft (see \ref Exodus 23:16|EXO 23:16\ref* and Exodus 34:22).\f* \v 17 \rb And should|וְ֠הָיָה\rb* \rb any|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb of the families|מִשְׁפְּח֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go up|יַעֲלֶ֜ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to worship|לְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֔ת\rb* \rb the King|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb*, \rb then the rain|הַגָּֽשֶׁם׃\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb fall|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 18 \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the people|מִשְׁפַּ֨חַת\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֧יִם\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go up|תַעֲלֶ֛ה\rb* \rb and|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb enter in|בָאָ֖ה\rb*, \rb then the rain will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb fall on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb this will be|תִּֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the plague|הַמַּגֵּפָ֗ה\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb strikes|יִגֹּ֤ף\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go up|יַֽעֲל֔וּ\rb* \rb to celebrate|לָחֹ֖ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Tabernacles|הַסֻּכּֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb will be|תִּהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the punishment|חַטַּ֣את\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |וְחַטַּאת֙\rb* \rb and of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go up|יַֽעֲל֔וּ\rb* \rb to celebrate|לָחֹ֖ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Tabernacles|הַסֻּכּֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb HOLY|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb TO THE LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 14:20 \ft That is, \fqa the LORD\f* \rb will be inscribed|יִֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bells|מְצִלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the horses|הַסּ֔וּס\rb*, \rb and the cooking pots|הַסִּירוֹת֙\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb like the sprinkling bowls|כַּמִּזְרָקִ֖ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb Indeed, every|כָּל־\rb* \rb pot|סִ֨יר\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb* \rb and Judah|וּבִֽיהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb will be|וְ֠הָיָה\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֚דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who sacrifice|הַזֹּ֣בְחִ֔ים\rb* \rb will come|וּבָ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb and take|וְלָקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb some pots|מֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and cook|וּבִשְּׁל֣וּ\rb* \rb in them|בָהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb And on that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb there will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb a Canaanite|כְנַעֲנִ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 14:21 \ft Or \fqa merchant\f* \rb in the house|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb*.
